The retained patch upgrades the core/base/relay graph to exactly 1.3.0,
requires rustls 0.23.45, exposes network_change, disable_port_mapping and
clear_ip_transports, and replaces the upstream network watcher notifier loop
with one endpoint-owned lazy netwatch monitor shared by cloned/protocol
handles. Explicit network_change calls notify both core and that monitor.
Android RouteMonitor is a no-op and netwatch suppresses equal interface
states, so Tokio watch preserves/coalesces actual Android connectivity hints
without polling. Closing the endpoint cancels network-watcher initialization
and in-flight callbacks and releases the shared monitor.
All five synchronous UniFFI watches (Connection.watch_paths/watch_path_events
and Endpoint.watch_addr/watch_home_relay/watch_network_change) register tasks
through one private WatchHandle.spawn, single-polling immediate registration
with UniFFI's existing async-compat Tokio runtime. No executor, runtime,
dependency, generated-Kotlin patch or public API change is added.
Connection close cancels pending path callbacks. Endpoint close cancels
address/home-relay stream waits and pending callbacks even while clones remain.
Stop and last-handle drop retain AbortOnDropHandle ownership and request abort;
they do not join or synchronously interrupt non-cooperative foreign callbacks.
Whole-connection shutdown does not guarantee final per-path Closed delivery.
The patch retains the explicit-network-hint regression and adds plain Rust
foreign-thread registration, actual loopback path callbacks and bounded
stop/drop/connection-close/endpoint-close cancellation regressions.
These regressions have not been executed by the patch worker.
No existing public binding API is removed. Kotlin is generated during the
Nix build by the UniFFI generator from the same retained FFI lock.

The Android context helper is copied, unchanged, from:
kotlin/android/src/main/kotlin/computer/iroh/IrohAndroid.kt
It and src/android_init.rs retain the upstream MIT/Apache-2.0 terms.
The source, patch and lock identities are in source.json; exact independently
resolved registry checksums, features and license declarations are in
dependencies.json. Its features describe Cargo metadata resolution across
workspace members/targets, not an executed Android build or advisory audit.
The runtime seam reuses locked UniFFI 0.31.2 (MPL-2.0), async-compat 0.2.6
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), n0-future 0.3.2 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), Tokio 1.53.2 and
tokio-util 0.7.19 (MIT); no dependency implementation is copied or modified.
Their original crate license/NOTICE files remain packaged by the native
producer. The FFI MIT/Apache-2.0 and Goatr GPL-3.0-or-later notices above remain.


